From a21bc0b3ab8e28bd8a6332a1f2725fbe745adec7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maciej=20Kr=C3=BCger?= <mkg20001@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:53:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] login: require acceptance of the terms of service and privacy
 policy

Before an OIDC/SAML flow completes, the user is sent to /legal when the
sha256 of the documents the instance's or org's legal settings link to
(fetched at runtime, LEGAL_DOCUMENT_TTL_SECONDS, default 300) differs
from the one in their user metadata key "agb"
(LEGAL_ACCEPTANCE_METADATA_KEY). Accepting there, or registering through
the register form, stores the current hash. prompt=none answers
consent_required. An unreachable document doesn't block sign-in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
